    "created_at": "2022-06-02T17:12:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-02T17:12:19Z",
    "body": "> I think that should be changed so that new render-blocking requests can be added if there are currently unresolved render-blocking requests, regardless of whether `document.body` exists.\r\n\r\nWe can do this specially for \"secondary\" requests (requests as a subresource of some element; not sure if we have a term for that).\r\n\r\nWe can't do it for HTML elements because it will otherwise widely affect the FCP of current pages.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1145105267/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
      "hooray": 0,
      "confused": 0,
