    "created_at": "2022-06-07T14:51:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-16T19:28:05Z",
    "body": "OK, I can see that render-blocking declarative markup should be in `head`. But for async scripts (that are themselves render-blocking) that call `fetch()` or `import()` or create a new classic `script`, it seems OK? `script` elements have a \"parser-inserted\" flag, so they could check `document.body` only if that flag is set.",
